 ## Overview
-This method optimizes hierarchical volume rendering by controlling the granularity of the coarse mesh used for bounding volume hierarchy (BVH) construction and macrocell-based optimizations. It solves the trade-off between BVH traversal efficiency and the overhead of traversing the underlying refinement tree (e.g., TET-AMR) by selecting which level of the refinement hierarchy is promoted to the coarse mesh [S1]. Unlike sibling methods that may use fixed coarse structures or different traversal primitives, this approach explicitly varies the refinement level inserted into the coarse mesh to balance macrocell tightness against BVH node count [S1].
